# The pre-commit hook formats and lints the files being committed. It cannot
# see whether the *repository* still works: a commit that breaks tsc, or a
# schema change that leaves a Zod schema behind, passes it without complaint
# and is found minutes later by CI — or, on a branch nobody opens a PR from,
# not at all.
#
# These are the two checks that are fast enough to sit in front of a push and
# broad enough to be worth it: typecheck (~4s) and the unit suite (~1s). The
# rest of the gate — build, pgTAP, Playwright — needs Docker or minutes, and
# belongs in CI where it already is.
#
# To push past it in an emergency: git push --no-verify
npm run typecheck
npm run test
